==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[High Priest Mamon]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*8 [[The Thrillerz]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*3 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 103.33~110 seconds<sup>3,100f~3,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**2 [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn, delay 1 second<sup>30f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bringing a Rich Cat item is almost necessary, as the stage is very hard without one.

Think of this stage as a stalling game. If you can keep Mamon away from your base while you deal with 5 Ragin' Gories, he won't be a threat anymore. You should therefore bring many fast meatshields and either [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or another anti-Dark attacker specifically for the Gories. If one has [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]], it can help stall Mamon and the Ragin' Gories, as it has a 30% chance to dodge Dark enemies, and can essentially form a wall if there is a stack of them. It may take a while, but even without shield piercing attacks, Mamon won't push too much if they're gone, and you'll ultimately win.

Bringing [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] is recommended, as Mamon comes with an absurd 1.800.000 HP shield, along with 3 knockbacks, Aku Researcher is fast enough to go in between Mamon's attack animation and land various hits if timed correctly. His [[True Form]] is highly recommended, as the drastic increase to attack rate that it provides may shorten the fight by several minutes.

[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] is not a bad choice. If you protect them well enough, they can end up pinning Mamon to the base, however, be careful, as their Crowd-Control only works if Mamon's shield is inactive. If you pair them with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and consistent shield piercing, Mamon's progression can be essentially halted.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]] is particularly effective in this stage thanks to his toxic and surge immunity, as well as his high damage shredding the support quickly.
*[[:Category: Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]] like [[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Lilin π]] and [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Hevijak the Wicked]] can help if your non-Uber piercers fail to get good procs in. However, most options are not long for this world, as Mamon's Toxic puts them out of commission rather quickly, [[Furiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Furilan Pasalan]] is most likely the best shield piercer here as he can actually survive and consistently break Mamon's shield thanks to his long range.
*Most [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]]/[[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] Ubers  will work wonders here, especially ones that target the main threats or are [[Toxic Immune]] such as [[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno]] (First or second form) or [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]].

